    <h2>Dispensaries in Bar Harbor & Mount Desert Island</h2>

    <h3>420 Mules — medical caregiver (delivery)</h3>
    <p><strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 801-0839<br>
    <strong>Registration:</strong> Maine medical caregiver — Michael J. Adelmann, dba 420 Mules (OCP caregiver roster, active through Jan 2027)<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP patients) — no adult-use store license in the OCP roster</p>
    <p><a href="/guides/420-mules-bar-harbor">420 Mules</a> is a registered Maine medical cannabis caregiver serving the Bar Harbor / Mount Desert Island area. The operator's own site describes the business as delivery of medicinal cannabis to registered patients; the OCP adult-use roster shows no storefront retail license, so walk-in recreational shopping is not something to count on. Some directories list a 224 Main St address, but hours and walk-in status are unverified — call or text 207-801-0839 before making the trip.</p>
    <p><strong>Visit:</strong> <a href="https://www.420mules.com/" data-cta-id="cta-referral-420-mules-bar-harbor" data-action-id="referral-420-mules-bar-harbor" data-action-family="cta_navigate" data-placement-id="city_guide" data-referral-kind="dispensary" data-partner-id="420-mules" data-referral-surface="city_guide">420mules.com</a></p>

    <h3>The Meristem — Southwest Harbor (the island's licensed adult-use store)</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 11 Seal Cove Road, Southwest Harbor, ME 04679<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 244-8789<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Tue–Sat 10am–6pm (closed Sun–Mon; confirm before visiting)<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Recreational (21+) and Medical — cash only, ATM on site<br>
    <strong>License:</strong> OCP adult-use store AMS600 (Meristem, LLC), active through Jun 2027</p>
    <p>The Meristem is on Mount Desert Island but in the town of <strong>Southwest Harbor</strong>, about 12 miles and a 20-minute drive from downtown Bar Harbor. Per the OCP adult-use roster it is the only active licensed adult-use store in Hancock County, and per the operator it was the first recreational retail shop in the county. Check in with valid ID at the side window. The location suits the quieter western side of the island and the Bass Harbor Head Light area — and it is roughly 26 minutes from the Hulls Cove visitor center.</p>
    <p><strong>Visit:</strong> <a href="https://themeristem.com/" data-cta-id="cta-referral-the-meristem-bar-harbor" data-action-id="referral-the-meristem-bar-harbor" data-action-family="cta_navigate" data-placement-id="city_guide" data-referral-kind="dispensary" data-partner-id="the-meristem" data-referral-surface="city_guide">themeristem.com</a></p>

    <h3>Snare Creek Farms — Trenton (medical)</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 211 Bar Harbor Rd, Trenton, ME 04605 (directories add Suite 3)<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 412-0209<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Mon–Sat 10am–6pm, Sun 10am–4pm (per snarecreekcannabis.com; confirm before visiting)<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP) — a valid medical ID is required<br>
    <strong>License:</strong> Registered medical caregiver (OCP roster, active through Dec 2026); adult-use application AMS1850 is still Pending Conditional, so no recreational sales yet</p>
    <p>Snare Creek Farms sits just over the mainland bridge from Mount Desert Island — about 16 miles and 27 minutes from downtown Bar Harbor — making it the first dispensary drivers encounter coming from the Ellsworth / US-1 corridor. Founded by an Air Force veteran and retired lobster-boat captain after 14 years as medical caregivers, it stocks indoor flower, concentrates, edibles, cartridges, and distillate from 17 vendors statewide. Its own site is explicit: this is a medical cannabis dispensary.</p>

    <h3>The Happier Choice — Trenton (medical caregiver)</h3>
    <p><strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP) — registered caregiver retail in Trenton (OCP caregiver roster: Judson M. Strang, dba The Happier Choice, active through Jan 2027)<br>
    <strong>Location:</strong> Bar Harbor Road, Trenton — local news reporting (May 2026) identifies it as a medicinal cannabis store on the Bar Harbor Road; directories list 169 Bar Harbor Rd</p>
    <p>A second medical option on the Trenton corridor for patients heading to the island. Confirm hours and address directly before visiting.</p>
