    <Faq
      questions={[
        { q: "Are there cannabis dispensaries in Bar Harbor, Maine?", a: "420 Mules is a registered medical caregiver serving Bar Harbor by delivery (no licensed storefront). For a licensed adult-use store, The Meristem in Southwest Harbor (11 Seal Cove Rd) is about 12 mi away. Medical-only options across the bridge in Trenton include Snare Creek Farms (211 Bar Harbor Rd) and The Happier Choice." },
        { q: "What is the closest dispensary to Acadia National Park?", a: "The Meristem (11 Seal Cove Rd, Southwest Harbor) is the closest licensed adult-use store to Acadia — about 26 minutes from the Hulls Cove visitor center. Snare Creek Farms in Trenton is about 24 minutes away but is medical-only (MMMP card required). Note that cannabis remains illegal inside Acadia: it is federal land." },
        { q: "Does Bar Harbor allow recreational cannabis?", a: "No — not locally. Maine legalized adult-use retail statewide, but Bar Harbor has not authorized it: voters rejected citizen-initiated retail ordinances at town meeting in June 2022 and again in November 2022, and the OCP records no retail authorization for the town. The nearest licensed recreational sales on Mount Desert Island are at The Meristem in Southwest Harbor; 420 Mules serves the town as a medical delivery caregiver." },
        { q: "Is 420 Mules in Bar Harbor recreational or medical?", a: "Medical. 420 Mules is a registered Maine medical cannabis caregiver (OCP caregiver roster: Michael J. Adelmann, dba 420 Mules, active through January 2027) delivering to registered MMMP patients. It holds no adult-use retail license in the OCP roster, so recreational walk-in sales are not available." },
        { q: "Do you need a medical card to buy cannabis near Bar Harbor?", a: "It depends on the store. The Meristem serves anyone 21+ with valid government-issued photo ID — no card needed. The medical-only stores (Snare Creek Farms and The Happier Choice in Trenton, and 420 Mules delivery) require a Maine medical cannabis card or a visiting-patient credential from a reciprocity state." },
        { q: "Can you buy cannabis in Bar Harbor without a Maine ID?", a: "Yes. Any valid government-issued photo ID proving you are 21+ works — an out-of-state driver's license or passport is accepted for recreational purchases at The Meristem. Maine residency is not required to buy adult-use cannabis." },
        { q: "Are Bar Harbor area dispensaries open year-round?", a: "Yes, the stores in this guide operate year-round, but hours shift with the tourism calendar and are worth confirming before a visit: The Meristem posts Tue–Sat 10am–6pm (closed Sun–Mon), Snare Creek Farms posts Mon–Sat 10am–6pm and Sun 10am–4pm, and 420 Mules delivery hours are set by appointment." },
        { q: "Can you consume cannabis in Acadia National Park?", a: "No. Acadia is federal land managed by the National Park Service, and cannabis remains illegal under federal law regardless of Maine's state rules. Consumption is prohibited throughout the park; use is limited to private property where the owner permits it." },
        { q: "What are the cannabis possession limits in Bar Harbor?", a: "Maine's statewide adult-use limits apply: up to 2.5 ounces of cannabis, or 2.5 ounces of a combination of cannabis and concentrate including no more than 10 grams of concentrate (28-B M.R.S. §1501(1)(B)). Public consumption is prohibited statewide." },
        { q: "Is there cannabis delivery in Bar Harbor?", a: "For medical patients, yes — 420 Mules is a registered caregiver delivering to MMMP patients in the Bar Harbor / MDI area. Adult-use delivery availability changes; check directly with The Meristem or the OCP's current adult-use rules before relying on it." },
        { q: "What is Bar Harbor, Maine known for?", a: "Bar Harbor is a coastal Hancock County town of 5,089 residents at the 2020 Census (5,352 est. 2025) on Mount Desert Island. It is the primary gateway community for Acadia National Park, which logged 3.96 million recreation visits in 2024 — Maine's most-visited tourism market." },
